@startuml
title DFSM fragment: memory states explode

[*] --> MEM_0
MEM_0 --> MEM_1 : M+ (store 1)
MEM_1 --> MEM_2 : M+ (store 2)
MEM_2 --> MEM_3 : M+ (store 3)

MEM_0 --> MEM_0 : MRC (display 0)
MEM_1 --> MEM_1 : MRC (display 1)
MEM_2 --> MEM_2 : MRC (display 2)
MEM_3 --> MEM_3 : MRC (display 3)

note right of MEM_3
  This pattern must continue for every possible
  stored value, so the DFSM needs an impractically
  large number of memory states.
end note
@enduml
